PELLETINO is released under the Zero-Clause BSD license (0BSD): no attribution,
no notice preservation, no conditions. It is meant to be free for everyone.

That covers the code written for this project: the launcher (main/), the shared
components (components/audio_hal, components/chiptune, components/display,
components/fest, components/imu, components/medalboot, components/mqart, and the
copies of them and of medal_input that each game carries under games/*/components/),
the build and asset tools (tools/), and the host harnesses (host/ and
games/*/host/).

It does NOT cover, and cannot relax the terms of, the third-party emulator cores
and libraries that individual games are built from, nor the game ROMs and
marquee art, none of which are distributed here. Each game under games/ carries
its own LICENSE and THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md, and the bundle as a whole is
described in LICENSING.md at the repository root. The most important consequence:
several cores are non-commercial only, so the assembled bundle may be shared
freely but not sold. See LICENSING.md before you distribute.

